 ## Overview
-This method converts pre-computed Signed Distance Field (SDF) data into a voxel grid suitable for Lattice Boltzmann Method (LBM) simulations, serving as an alternative to runtime STL mesh voxelization [S1, unofficial]. It leverages GPU-accelerated trilinear interpolation to produce smoother solid boundaries compared to ray-casting STL triangles, and offers performance benefits for complex geometries that are reused across multiple simulations [S1, unofficial]. It builds on [SDF Grid Resampling from File](4878-sdf-grid-resampling-from-file.md) by defining the specific binary format and GPU kernel logic for this particular SDF variant.
+This method converts pre-computed Signed Distance Field (SDF) data into a voxel grid suitable for Lattice Boltzmann Method (LBM) simulations, serving as an alternative to runtime STL mesh voxelization [S1, unofficial]. It leverages GPU-accelerated trilinear interpolation to produce smoother solid boundaries compared to ray-casting STL triangles, and offers performance benefits for complex geometries that are reused across multiple simulations [S1, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
 **Inputs and Outputs**
-*   **Input:** A binary SDF file containing grid dimensions, bounding box, and distance values; a target scale (LBM units); an optional center position; and an optional 3x3 rotation matrix [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Input:** A binary SDF file containing grid dimensions, bounding box, and distance values; a target scale in LBM units; an optional center position; and an optional 3×3 rotation matrix [S1, unofficial].
