 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls**
-*   **Out-of-Bounds Sampling:** If the transformed coordinate falls outside the SDF grid bounds, coordinates must be clamped to the nearest grid edge to prevent memory access violations [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Rotation Inversion:** The kernel requires the inverse of the provided rotation matrix. If the input matrix is not orthogonal, the inverse may not equal the transpose, leading to incorrect orientation [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Precision:** Trilinear interpolation smooths the sharp boundaries of the original mesh, which is a feature, not a bug, but may slightly alter the effective volume of the solid [S1, unofficial].
